  "summary": "Recent preprints use mathematical and simulation models to test how menopause, cell division control and somatic mutation shape tissue-level dynamics.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is model-based inference of how cellular and tissue-level states change over time. The MSCE-T model attributes the Clemmesen's hook in breast cancer incidence to menopausal shifts in early mutant-cell proliferation and apoptosis. A piecewise deterministic Markov chain with maximum likelihood inference estimates cell size regulation division parameters, and a rule-based multi-level simulation of beta-cell mitochondrial fission probes how Fis1, MFF and Drp1 affect glycolysis, OXPHOS and insulin secretion. These studies do not share one mechanism, so the thread is dominant rather than universal. What is new is the survival model treating somatic mutation accumulation as an entropic upper bound on human lifespan, with post-mitotic neurons and cardiomyocytes as bottlenecks.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-30"
